# UI Performance & Rebuild Rules

## Rebuild scope
- ✅ Keep `Consumer`/`ref.watch` as low as possible in the widget tree
- ✅ Split large screens into smaller widgets to reduce rebuild blast radius
- ✅ Use selectors (`select`) for watching small slices of state

## Lists
- ✅ Use `ListView.builder` / `SliverList` for large lists
- ✅ Keep list item widgets cheap and mostly const
- ✅ Avoid measuring/layout hacks (no unnecessary IntrinsicHeight/Width)

## Images
- ✅ Use caching/network image strategy (document package choice)
- ✅ Provide placeholders and error states

## Async UI
- ✅ Prefer `AsyncValue` patterns (loading/error/data)
- ✅ Don’t re-fetch on every rebuild (cache/keepAlive as needed)

## NEVER
- ❌ Do expensive parsing/JSON decoding in build
- ❌ Use nested scroll views without clear reason
